sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength of Gasterosteus doryssus_early at 33 µm (10.02 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 87.2/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 closes R1–R3. Successor doryssus_mid PDE wavelength is 43.11 µm (analytic 41.71 µm), longer than the early nonlinear wavelength 33.87 µm. Four seeds give λ = 33.87, 32.77, 33.17, 34.46 µm, CV = 0.0223. At fixed D_u, σ_max is -0.085 when D_v/D_u = 1 and +0.186 at the locked ratio 12.277; above threshold λ lengthens from 30.47 µm (ratio 8.5) to 39.20 µm (ratio 28). Dispersion Pearson r remains 0.9947. GIF CV remains 85.9 on 12 frames at 640×480. Gallery high-pass band remains 81.08 µm. Overall 87.2/100 (faithfulness 86.4, reproducibility 89.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 89, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/gasterosteus_doryssus_early_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 334104 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 7b732f95bd42a0cbbce83ed9d5633db03d86db236221e2d704d532502109fad1 (sha256 7b732f95bd42a0cbbce83ed9d5633db03d86db236221e2d704d532502109fad1), spec_fingerprint 7da029c4116b272894d7e1440005167263445ac99716f78586b6bac5b2bee85e. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 7da029c4116b272894d7e1440005167263445ac99716f78586b6bac5b2bee85e; artifact_sha256: 7b732f95bd42a0cbbce83ed9d5633db03d86db236221e2d704d532502109fad1. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion relation and Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics. | Hunt, Bell & Travis (2008) and Bell, Travis & Blouw (2006): pelvic reduction along the Truckee G. doryssus series, complete pelvis at the start. | Stuart, Travis & Bell (2020): Pitx1 in that fossil lineage. Nakamasu et al. (2009) and Kondo & Miura (2010): teleost chromatophore Turing patterns.; reconstructed_in_script: Early-chronospecies Schnakenberg field at λ near 32.86 µm, equal-diffusion ablation, D_u sweep, diffusion-ratio sweep, four-seed ensemble, and a successor integration at D_u × (41.50/32.86)^2. | m=2 ocellus GIF whose amplitude follows RMS(u), CV 85.9 against the gallery photograph.; transfer_boundary: 32.86 µm is the assigned cellular-detail rung, not a spacing published by Bell, Hunt, or Stuart. | The successor diffusivity scaling is a model of wavelength lengthening tied to pelvic reduction, not a measurement at 10.01 Ma. | The gallery spiral is not a Truckee thin section. Its 81.08 µm band is not λ_c.; does_not_claim: An emergent PDE spiral, a second assessor, a machine-checked Lean build, or a signed nanopublication.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Lean 4 is not installed in this image, so the six decide-theorems were not executed.",
            "remediation needed: R4 remains open: a second assessor from another provider has not scored this slot.",
            "remediation needed: The GIF carrier is still an imposed m=2 spiral. Replacing it with a PDE-emergent spiral would have to keep CV similarity at or above 58.",
            "remediation needed: The gallery photograph is still a project spiral, not a Truckee Formation thin section. A CC fossil image at this scale was not found." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.872"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; second assessor still absent)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

